Stop the RADIUS client from linking a Windows SDK library member into postgres.exe.

The assignment copies the all-zero IPv6 address over a structure that the memset two lines
earlier has already zeroed, so deleting it changes no behaviour. On Windows, its reference
to in6addr_any is the only reason the linker copies a member of a Windows SDK static library,
ws2_32.lib(indef.obj), into the archive. See "Source patches" in docs/native-artifact.md.

Remove this patch with the move to PostgreSQL 19, which no longer has RADIUS support
(upstream commit a1643d40b3).

--- a/src/backend/libpq/auth.c
+++ b/src/backend/libpq/auth.c
@@ -3065,7 +3065,6 @@
 
 	memset(&localaddr, 0, sizeof(localaddr));
 	localaddr.sin6_family = serveraddrs[0].ai_family;
-	localaddr.sin6_addr = in6addr_any;
 	if (localaddr.sin6_family == AF_INET6)
 		addrsize = sizeof(struct sockaddr_in6);
 	else
